{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"bdd29fac55ca42c0","name":"card_event_free_french_navy","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/events/card_event_free_french_navy","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FREE FRENCH NAVY","text":"Draw the top unit of your deck with an operation cost of 3. Your HQ gains +3 defense.","flavorText":"The Free French Navy (Forces Navales Françaises Libres, FNFL) played a significant role in WWII after the fall of France in 1940. The Free French Navy began with a small force of about 3,600 sailors and 50 vessels, led by Vice-Admiral Émile Muselier who was the only flag officer of the French Navy to join the Free French Forces. As the war progressed its ranks and fleet grew, as more sailors and ships aligned with De Gaulle’s Free France joined from overseas colonies. The Free French Navy operated in various theaters, from the North Atlantic to the Mediterranean, and supported key operations such as the Battle of the Atlantic, the Normandy and Provence landings, and the liberation of French territories.","faction":"France","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_free_french_navy","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_free_french_navy_title","SourceString":"FREE FRENCH NAVY","LocalizedString":"FREE FRENCH NAVY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_free_french_navy_text","SourceString":"Draw the top unit of your deck with an operation cost of 3. Your HQ gains +3 defense.","LocalizedString":"Draw the top unit of your deck with an operation cost of 3. Your HQ gains +3 defense."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_free_french_navy_history","SourceString":"The Free French Navy (Forces Navales Françaises Libres, FNFL) played a significant role in WWII after the fall of France in 1940. The Free French Navy began with a small force of about 3,600 sailors and 50 vessels, led by Vice-Admiral Émile Muselier who was the only flag officer of the French Navy to join the Free French Forces. As the war progressed its ranks and fleet grew, as more sailors and ships aligned with De Gaulle’s Free France joined from overseas colonies. The Free French Navy operated in various theaters, from the North Atlantic to the Mediterranean, and supported key operations such as the Battle of the Atlantic, the Normandy and Provence landings, and the liberation of French territories.","LocalizedString":"The Free French Navy (Forces Navales Françaises Libres, FNFL) played a significant role in WWII after the fall of France in 1940. The Free French Navy began with a small force of about 3,600 sailors and 50 vessels, led by Vice-Admiral Émile Muselier who was the only flag officer of the French Navy to join the Free French Forces. As the war progressed its ranks and fleet grew, as more sailors and ships aligned with De Gaulle’s Free France joined from overseas colonies. The Free French Navy operated in various theaters, from the North Atlantic to the Mediterranean, and supported key operations such as the Battle of the Atlantic, the Normandy and Provence landings, and the liberation of French territories."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/Winter_2024/t_free_french_navy.t_free_french_navy","SubPathString":""},"artist":"French WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FREE_FRENCH_NAVY.FREE_FRENCH_NAVY","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":386.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_free_french_navy_photo","SourceString":"General De 